<http://data.silknow.org/object/80099b28-34fd-393a-82ee-a84eafa043be>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "A man’s coat of pale blue silk taffeta with a 1¼-inch (3.2 cm) standing collar and curving 2-piece sleeves end in cuffs 4 inches (10cm) deep.  The fronts curve from neck to hem with pleats 4½-inch (11.4 cm) deep, below the hip set at the side back.  Each front has a pocket with scalloped pocket flap; the centre-back seam is open below the hip.   The coat and pocket flaps are lined with ivory silk twill, the sleeves and pockets with bleached linen.  \n\nThe coat was probably worn for fancy dress in the late 19th century. Machine-made lace cuffs were added; the original buttons removed and replaced with cut-steel buttons.  The black silk wig bag was stitched to the back neck."@en , "Man's coat, 1775-1780, British; Pale blue silk taffeta, altered 1870-1910"@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/05d85f60-16e0-30bf-b612-cf4bd1126288> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/3b5aa0e6-9643-3daa-904f-ecdc76123ce4> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/9b379f02-6d33-3db0-b5f4-f07914a15c85> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/c20d97a0-7f22-34cf-9a5f-ad868648435e> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Man's coat, 1775-1780, British; Pale blue silk taffeta, altered 1870-1910"@en , "A man’s coat of pale blue silk taffeta with a 1¼-inch (3.2 cm) standing collar and curving 2-piece sleeves end in cuffs 4 inches (10cm) deep.  The fronts curve from neck to hem with pleats 4½-inch (11.4 cm) deep, below the hip set at the side back.  Each front has a pocket with scalloped pocket flap; the centre-back seam is open below the hip.   The coat and pocket flaps are lined with ivory silk twill, the sleeves and pockets with bleached linen.  \n\nThe coat was probably worn for fancy dress in the late 19th century. Machine-made lace cuffs were added; the original buttons removed and replaced with cut-steel buttons.  The black silk wig bag was stitched to the back neck."@en ;
        ecrm:P43_has_dimension         <http://data.silknow.org/object/80099b28-34fd-393a-82ee-a84eafa043be/dimension/1> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/80099b28-34fd-393a-82ee-a84eafa043be/dimension/2> ;
        dc:identifier                  "T.16-1950" ;
